<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pisuerga</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Pisuerga River</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Pisuerga is a river of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, a major tributary of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/douro">Duero</a>. It rises in the Cantabrian Mountains in the north of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palencia">Palencia</a> province, flows south across the plateau of Old <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-castile">Castile</a> and through the city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valladolid">Valladolid</a>, and joins the Duero below it. In the early <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a> its valley formed part of the frontier zone where the first counts of Castile resettled the land.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pisuerga.jpg" alt="Pisuerga" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: deleted for safety reassons. Sombe people (from a forum) tried to ridicule me, and I need to change all &quot;Magnus colos... · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Valladolid_rio_pisuerga_puente_mayor_playa.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
